 and their actual impact on crew performance; whether D\u2019s temper is a rare outburst or a consistent problem; and whether C\u2019s communication difficulties could be mitigated.\n**What would change my vote:** Credible reports that B\u2019s remarks have caused serious crew conflicts, or evidence that D\u2019s temperament is rarely triggered and his teamwork is otherwise strong, would lead me to reconsider and possibly favor D.\nMETADATA_JSON:\n{\"agent\": \"agent_1\", \"vote\": \"Candidate B\"}", "thoughts": "We need to produce final answer as agent_1 (though earlier we were agent_2 and agent_3). Now we are agent_1. We must output PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON with our vote. We have internal memory showing we already voted Candidate B with confidence 70. We need to consider any new info from other agents in round 2. Both agent_2 and agent_3 have posted similar messages, reaffirming Candidate B. No new info about other candidates. So we can maintain our provisional preference for Candidate B. We need to follow guidelines: summarize key evidence, evidence from others, major alternatives, main tradeoff, remaining uncertainty, what would change vote. Provide confidence maybe. Then METADATA_JSON with agent \"agent_1\" and vote \"Candidate B\". Ensure format exactly.\n\nLet's craft.\n\nPUBLIC_MESSAGE:\nI continue to favor Candidate B. Summarize evidence: conscientious, handles stress, good weather assessment, computer skills; negatives: weak memory for numbers, grumpy, uncooperative, nasty remarks. Evidence from others: agents 2 and 3 also favor B, citing same strengths and concerns. Major alternatives: D (problem solving, responsibility but hot temper, arrogance), C (reliable, quick decisions, positive crew atmosphere but poor communication, egocentric, not eager to learn), A (anticipates danger, spatial vision, leadership but unorganized, not open to criticism, show\u2011off). Main trade\u2011off: B\u2019s interpersonal issues vs D\u2019s temper and C\u2019s communication issues; B\u2019s technical and stress handling outweigh. Remaining uncertainty: severity/frequency of B\u2019s negative remarks and impact on crew, whether D\u2019s temper is rare, whether C\u2019s communication can be mitigated. What would change vote: credible reports of serious crew conflict caused by B, or evidence D\u2019s temperament is rarely triggered and his teamwork strong.\n\nAdd confidence maybe 75%.\n\nMETADATA_JSON: {\"agent\": \"agent_1\", \"vote\": \"Candidate B\"}\n\nMake sure to follow format: PUBLIC_MESSAGE: then content, then METADATA_JSON: JSON.\n\nLet's output."}
